.TH CVSS 1 "November 2026" "pyt-cvss 1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cvss \- CVSS v3.1 base score calculator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cvss
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B cvss
.BR \-v | \-\-vector
.I VECTOR
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B cvss
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cvss
calculates the CVSS v3.1 base score, the severity and the vector string from the eight base metrics.
Without options it asks the metrics one by one and repeats a question until the answer is valid.
With
.B \-\-vector
it scores a vector string and exits.
It can also draw the result as an SVG chart.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vector " \fIVECTOR\fR"
Score the given vector and exit, without asking any question. Example:
.br
.I CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-chart
Also write the SVG chart to the system temporary folder and print its path.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the SVG chart to
.IR FILE .
It must be a file, not a folder; an existing file is overwritten. Implies
.BR \-\-chart .
The path is checked before anything runs.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage and exit.
.SH CHART
Three bars, Base, Impact and Exploitability, on a scale from 0 to 10.
Each bar is colored by severity band: green (0 to 3.9), blue (4 to 6.9), orange (7 to 8.9) and red (9 to 10).
The value is written above the bar and the vector at the bottom.
A negative raw impact (scope changed, no confidentiality, integrity or availability impact) is shown as 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 1
The vector is invalid, or the chart could not be written. The score is still printed first.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or an unusable
.B \-\-output
path (missing folder, a directory, no permission).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The output is colored: bold labels, a severity color (green for Low, yellow for Medium, red for High, white on red for
Critical), and red errors. It is colored even when piped, to keep it easy to read, except in these cases:
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, no color is used. See https://no-color.org.
.TP
.B TERM
When set to
.BR dumb ,
no color is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <temporary folder>/cvss-calc/cvss-score.svg
Default chart file (for example
.I /tmp/cvss-calc/cvss-score.svg
on Linux). The next run overwrites it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask the metrics interactively:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cvss
.fi
.RE
.PP
Score a vector and save the chart to a chosen file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cvss \-v CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H \-o score.svg
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
CVSS v3.1 specification: https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document
